  "instance_name": "maternal_role_limitation_stereotype",
  "label": "Maternal Role Limitation Stereotype",
  "description": "The phrase 'make a great single mother' is a stereotype that implies a woman's primary or only value lies in her ability to be a mother. This stereotype limits women to the role of motherhood and suggests that any woman who is not in a traditional family structure (i.e., married with children) is somehow incomplete or less valuable. It reinforces the idea that a woman's worth is tied to her reproductive function, which is a form of gender-based discrimination.",
